# .claude/effort-verdict — recorded output of the effort A/B interference test.
#
# WHAT: the single effort level a real working session should launch at.
# WHO CONSUMES IT:
#   - `make session`  -> exec claude --effort <first-non-comment-line>
#   - .claude/scripts/session-start.sh Warning 4, which reconciles this
#     verdict against the live session effort and the effortLevel floor.
# HOW IT IS PRODUCED: docs/EFFORT-AB-TEST.md, executed under the paid,
#   cost-gated task claude-workflow-plugin-cnz.2 (NOT cnz.1).
#
# FORMAT: the first non-comment, non-blank line is the verdict. Valid values:
#   max        — persistable everywhere; the safe default.
#   ultracode  — session-only (claude --effort ultracode); adds dynamic
#                workflow orchestration but cannot be pinned in settings.
# ultracode's hook-env proxy is xhigh, so a session launched at ultracode is
# indistinguishable from a plain xhigh session inside the hooks — session-start
# is honest about that.
max
